<title>JAPAN: Swedish mortgage firm sets terms of samurai bonds.</title>
<headline>Swedish mortgage firm sets terms of samurai bonds.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-11-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Daiwa Securities Co Ltd announced on Monday terms of the first yen/dollar dual-currency samurai bonds issued by Venantius AB, the Swedish National Mortgage Agency.</p>
<p>The coupon was set at 4.85 percent and the 20 billion yen bonds, priced at par, will mature on June 6, 2000.</p>
</text>
